Derived fields have now been implemented in the dungeon generator. I introduced a `derived_fields` dictionary to each `CellColumn` to store arbitrary metrics, then added a BFS-based routine to compute the Manhattan distance from every cell to the nearest wall. I also compute an “openness” score for each walkable cell by counting its walkable neighbors and assign simple affordance tags—`space.open_arena`, `space.choke`, or `space.normal`—based on that score. These tags and metrics will inform later systems like spawning and AI.

