I've enhanced the generator with several new capabilities:

- **Varied room shapes**: Rooms are now randomly rectangular, rounded (elliptical), or L‑shaped. Each room stores its shape and orientation, and carving uses the appropriate mask.
- **Door placement & distance fields**: After carving, corridor cells adjacent to exactly one room are converted to doors (`DOOR` base) and tagged with `threshold.door`. The derived-field computation now also calculates distance to the nearest door so spawn logic can use it.
- **Improved spawn solver**: The solver supports new constraints (`allowed_room_ids`, `min_distance_to_spawn`) and can now place hazards and quest objects in addition to enemies and items. Hazard spawns respect a separate budget, avoid clustering, and prefer tighter spaces; a single quest item is placed in a random room (excluding the starting room). Spawns can still specify preferences across derived fields and random noise.

